            IPC Table 709.1 — DFU values and trap sizes
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            Rendered from the same data the calculator uses, so the two cannot disagree. Fixtures with no trap
            size shown have an integral trap.
          </p>

          <div class="mt-8 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white shadow-sm">
            <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
              <thead>
                <tr class="border-b border-slate-200 text-slate-500 bg-slate-50">
                  <th class="py-3 px-5 font-semibold">Fixture</th>
                  <th class="py-3 px-5 font-semibold">DFU</th>
                  <th class="py-3 px-5 font-semibold">Min trap</th>
                  <th class="py-3 px-5 font-semibold">Type</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody class="text-slate-700">
                {
                  DFU_FIXTURES.map((f, index) => (
                    <tr class={index === DFU_FIXTURES.length - 1 ? "" : "border-b border-slate-100"}>
                      <td class="py-3 px-5 font-semibold text-slate-900">{f.label}</td>
                      <td class="py-3 px-5">{fmt(f.dfu, f.dfu % 1 === 0 ? 0 : 1)}</td>
                      <td class="py-3 px-5">{f.trap === null ? "integral" : sizeLabel(f.trap)}</td>
                      <td class="py-3 px-5 text-slate-500">{f.group}</td>
                    </tr>
                  ))
                }
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <h2 class="mt-14 text-3xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-slate-900">
            IPC Table 709.2 — fixtures not otherwise listed
          </h2>
          <p class="mt-4 text-slate-600 leading-relaxed">
            When a fixture is not in Table 709.1, its drain connection decides its value.
          </p>

          <div class="mt-8 overflow-x-auto rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white shadow-sm">
            <table class="w-full text-left text-sm">
              <thead>
                <tr class="border-b border-slate-200 text-slate-500 bg-slate-50">
                  <th class="py-3 px-5 font-semibold">Drain connection</th>
                  <th class="py-3 px-5 font-semibold">DFU value</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody class="text-slate-700">
                {
                  DFU_BY_DRAIN_SIZE.map((row, index) => (
                    <tr class={index === DFU_BY_DRAIN_SIZE.length - 1 ? "" : "border-b border-slate-100"}>
                      <td class="py-3 px-5 font-semibold text-slate-900">{sizeLabel(row.size)}</td>
                      <td class="py-3 px-5">{row.dfu}</td>
                    </tr>
                  ))
                }
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>

          <p class="mt-6 text-sm text-slate-500">
            Sources &amp; standards: <a
              class="underline hover:text-emerald-600"
              href="https://codes.iccsafe.org/codes/i-codes"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener">IPC</a
            > 2021 Table 709.1 (drainage fixture unit values), Table 709.2 (fixtures not listed), Table 710.1(1)
            (building drains and sewers) and Table 710.1(2) (horizontal branches and stacks), including the
            footnote setting a 3-inch minimum on a building drain serving a water closet. Roughly fifteen
            states use the <a
              class="underline hover:text-emerald-600"
              href="https://www.iapmo.org/uniform-plumbing-code"
              target="_blank"
              rel="noopener">UPC</a
            > or a derivative, which assigns some fixtures different values. Local amendments override the
            model code.
          </p>
        </div>
      </section>

